# Code owners for ml-party.
#
# Gates who must approve changes to security-sensitive paths. Note that
# CODEOWNERS only *blocks a merge* when branch protection on `main` has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. That setting is currently
# OFF, because with a single maintainer it would block every PR (nobody
# can approve their own). It is listed here so the ownership is declared,
# review requests route correctly, and the rule becomes enforceable the
# moment a second maintainer exists. Until then the load-bearing gates
# are: merging requires write access, and the agent-instruction guard
# workflow. See SECURITY.md.

# --- Agent-instruction files -------------------------------------------
# Read and ACTED ON by AI coding agents working in this repo. A malicious
# edit is prompt injection against contributors' own agents, not against
# the shipped package.
/AGENTS.md      @paul-krug
/CLAUDE.md      @paul-krug
/.agents/       @paul-krug
**/SKILL.md     @paul-krug

# --- Shipped agent instructions ----------------------------------------
# The MCP server's instruction text travels in the wheel to every agent
# connected to any ml-party store — the widest-reach instruction surface
# in the repo.
/src/mlparty/mcp_server.py  @paul-krug

# --- The gates themselves ----------------------------------------------
# Owning .github/** keeps an attacker from editing the gate open in the
# same PR, and covers release.yml — which publishes to PyPI under this
# project's trusted-publisher identity. Keep last so it wins for
# everything under .github/.
/.github/       @paul-krug
